### [`tone2`]($section.id('tone2').attrs('doc-entry'))

Plays a sound tone via the hardware buzzer. Cancels any other audio that might
be playing. Sends CART_TONE IPC to kernel; kernel plays via gpio.buzzer or
I2S depending on board revision.

- Return Type: void
- Arguments:
  - options: [ToneOptions](#tone2-options)

### [`set_global_volume`]($section.id('set-global-volume').attrs('doc-entry'))

Adjust the volume of all audio, 0.0 - 1.0. This is a perceptually linear scale
from about -50dB to 0dB adjustment from the maximum speaker volume.

- Return Type: void
- Arguments:
  - volume: f32

### [`rand`]($section.id('rand').attrs('doc-entry'))

Returns a random number from the RP2350 ring oscillator random bit.
Useful for seeding a faster PRNG.

- Return Type: u32
- Arguments: none

### [`trace`]($section.id('trace').attrs('doc-entry'))

Prints a message to the debug console. On native: copies string to shared buffer
and sends CART_TRACE via FIFO; kernel prints to UART. Used by Blobs and other
carts for panic/debug output.

- Return Type: void
- Arguments:
  - x: []const u8

### [`present`]($section.id('present').attrs('doc-entry'))

Signal Core 0 that the framebuffer is ready and wait for the LCD flush to
complete before returning.

Call this once per frame (typically at the end of update().attrs('doc-entry')). On WASM this is a
no-op because the simulator owns the display.

- Return Type: void
- Arguments: none

### [`read_flash`]($section.id('read-flash').attrs('doc-entry'))

Attempts to fill dst, returns the amount of bytes actually read.
NOTE: No dedicated cart save-data flash region exists yet; returns 0.

- Return Type: u32
- Arguments:
  - offset: u32
  - dst: []u8

### [`write_flash_page`]($section.id('write-flash-page').attrs('doc-entry'))

NOTE: No dedicated cart save-data flash region exists yet; this is a no-op stub.

- Return Type: void
- Arguments:
  - page: u16
  - src: \[flash_page_size\]u8

